WEBVTT

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.500
Yusei only has Junk Archer on his field, which 
isn't enough to defeat Andore's three monsters!

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.090
Yusei must have a strategy in mind!

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.820
Yusei...

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:10.350
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.890
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.470
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:26.130
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.170
There's no need to fear

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:38.810
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.950
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.590
Streak to the infinite future

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:56.180
Dreams surpass their limits

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:04.100
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:36.030
Beyond Despair and Conflict...

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:48.470
Battle!  Green Baboon attacks Junk Archer!

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.680
Hammer Club Death!

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.650
I activate the trap Chain Arrow!

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.550
During damage calculation, Junk 
Archer gains 500 attack points.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.320
What?

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:10.120
Since Junk Archer has Chain Arrow's effect 
and destroyed a monster in battle...

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:15.060
...your monster loses 1000 attack 
points until this turn's End Phase!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.180
I can no longer attack.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:36.590
All right!  Junk Archer isn't destroyed, 
and Behemoth lost attack points!

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.540
He can't destroy Junk Archer 
with his two remaining monsters!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.930
You did it, Yusei!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.540
Yusei is incredible.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.020
Chain Arrow's effect ends, and Junk 
Archer's attack points return to normal.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.600
He survived.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.540
On the last turn, Yusei 
knew that Green Baboon,

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.450
which Junk Archer's effect removed from 
play, would return at the End Phase.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.610
That's why he had a trap ready to 
counteract Green Baboon's attack.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.690
Well done.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:17.130
Yusei, I said that your card playing 
skills had flaws, but I was wrong!

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.800
I take back what I said, and 
I'll apologize with this!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.530
I activate the trap Beast Burial Ritual!

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.140
I destroy one monster on my field and send 
it to the graveyard to draw two cards!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.640
I destroy Nimble Momonga!

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.030
He destroyed his own monster again.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.220
That means...

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.950
When a Beast-Type monster is destroyed...

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:49.190
I can Special Summon Green Baboon from 
my graveyard by paying 1000 life points!

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.080
It appeared again!

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.330
This is bad!  Junk Archer's attack points 
have already returned to its original points!

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.030
It's amazing that Andore had that trap ready.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.790
Andore is impressive.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:06.240
In the last battle, you would usually attack

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.310
with Behemoth instead of Green Baboon 
because it has more attack points.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.050
But Andore used his intuition and 
attacked with Green Baboon first.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.870
Therefore, he turned the tables 
on Chain Arrow's effect

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.920
and sent Green Baboon to the graveyard.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:29.980
If he attacked with Behemoth first, he 
couldn't have resurrected Green Baboon.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:30.930
I see.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:37.900
Andore's card playing intuition 
surpasses Yusei's calculated combos.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.340
Battle!  Green Baboon attacks Junk Archer!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.420
Next, Behemoth attacks you directly!

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.920
Take this, Yusei!

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.410
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:04.900
Chain Arrow's effect vanishes, so Behemoth's 
attack points return to normal.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.040
I was planning to finish you this 
turn, but you managed to survive.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.270
Now it's your turn!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.680
It's time for your counterattack, Yusei!

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.750
My turn!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.490
I summon Shield Wing in defense position!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.770
I'll use it to survive for now.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.830
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.830
He's not going to counterattack?

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.610
He can't easily counterattack 
in this situation.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.070
Can't you tell by watching?

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:46.040
That's right.  He has to survive for now.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:52.150
Yusei shouldn't be struggling because 
he's used to battling my power deck!

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.510
It means that his opponent is very powerful.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.980
Don't worry!

00:06:55.980 --> 00:07:01.320
Shield Wing is a powerful defense monster 
that can survive two attacks per turn!

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:07.290
Even if he summons a third monster next 
turn, he can't attack Yusei directly!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.740
I don't think he'll defeat him anytime soon.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.890
You're wrong.  Andore is about to end this.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.530
Because if he goes too easy on him, 
they're going to get suspicious.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.690
It's time to finish this duel.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.800
My turn!

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.810
I summon Nimble Momonga!

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:31.610
I send a Beast-Type monster 
in my hand to the graveyard

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.200
to Special Summon the Tuner 
Monster Egotistical Ape!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.200
Egotistical Ape's Level increases 
by the Level of the monster

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.470
that was sent to the graveyard!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.190
A fourth monster!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:53.020
Shield Wing has a mere 900 defense points!

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.680
If three monsters attack, 
Shield Wing will be destroyed!

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.280
Yusei will lose if he takes a direct 
attack from a fourth monster!

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.240
Oh no!

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.110
I activate the trap Shield Coat!

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:12.800
When you Special Summon a monster who's 
stronger than my defending monster's defense points...

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.670
...my monster's defense points are doubled!

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.710
All right!  Now the two monsters other than

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:23.130
Green Baboon and Behemoth 
can't destroy Shield Wing!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:29.110
Level 7 Egotistical Ape tunes 
Level 2 Nimble Momonga!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.080
When the wild blood flows mix, the 
power to sever the land awakens!

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.920
Roar!

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.210
Synchro Summon!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.880
Nature's power, Naturia Gaodrake!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.280
3000 attack points!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:51.710
He immediately reacted to Shield Wing's 
increased defense points and changed his strategy!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:55.760
But Shield Wing can stop up to three attacks!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.100
Battle!  Green Baboon attacks Shield Wing!

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.950
Behemoth attacks next!

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.480
I'm not done!  I attack for a 
third time with Naturia Gaodrake!

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.990
Shield Wing is destroyed!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:24.460
Don't worry.  He has no 
monsters left to attack with.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.630
It's too early to feel safe!

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.430
I activate the trap Howl of the Wild!

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:35.270
When my Beast-Type monster destroys 
your monster in battle...

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.870
...you take 300 points of damage for 
every Beast-Type monster on my field!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:40.870
What?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:45.610
There are three Beast-Types on my 
field!  Take 900 points of damage!

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:53.250
I set one card and end my turn.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:57.220
Yusei is quickly down to 300 life points!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.290
And he doesn't have any monsters.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.460
He's incredible!

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.930
Andore is exceptional!

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.080
Such high-level dueling...

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.900
Is this what a battle between D-Wheelers 
entering the tournament is like?

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.340
I know that Yusei will make a comeback!

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.080
My turn!

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:31.360
All right!

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.390
I summon Debris Dragon!

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.280
When I successfully summon Debris Dragon...

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:45.000
I can Special Summon one monster with 500-or-fewer 
attack points from my graveyard in attack position.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.300
Come, Shield Wing!

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:58.860
Since I have 2-or-more Speed Counters, 
I activate Speed Spell - Vision Wind!

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.290
I Special Summon one Level 2-or-below 
monster from my graveyard!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.050
Come, Speed Warrior!

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:15.560
Level 4 Debris Dragon tunes Level 2 
Speed Warrior and Level 2 Shield Wing!

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.250
The wishes come together 
to form a new shining star!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.960
Become the path that lights the way!

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:25.640
Synchro Summon!

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.780
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.530
Stardust Dragon!

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:52.000
His ace monster finally arrived.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.250
I didn't think it was going to appear.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.970
What will he show us?

00:11:56.970 --> 00:12:00.940
Battle!  Stardust Dragon 
attacks Green Baboon!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:06.150
Have you lost your mind?  Green 
Baboon has higher attack points.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.020
I activate my trap Synchro Strike!

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:14.940
Stardust Dragon gains 500 attack points 
for every Synchro Material Monster!

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:17.590
What?  4000 attack points?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.060
Shooting Sonic!

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.100
He did it!

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.570
He has more life points than him!

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:30.360
Yusei has more than 4 Speed Counters.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:35.420
If he has a Speed Spell in his hand, he can 
use its effect to make Andore have 0 life points!

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:38.570
Aki, you're starting to understand.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.550
That makes you a D-Wheeler!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.980
Ten, nine, eight...

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.350
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:53.460
For every Speed Spell in my hand, 
you take 800 points of damage!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:53.460
Two, one, zero!

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.340
What?

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.800
Practice is over.  This duel is suspended.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.010
That was nice dueling.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.250
Yeah, you too.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.540
We'll settle this during the tournament.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.550
Bye.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.380
Yusei!

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.490
You were so close!  You almost won!

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:23.720
No.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.690
He still had a set card on his field.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.930
Knowing him, I doubt that card was a bluff.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.490
So he still had another strategy ready?

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:35.720
Most likely.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.170
If you continued to duel, you 
could've been in trouble.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.310
Team Unicorn is a fearsome opponent.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.780
They might become our greatest rival.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.750
I'm stronger than them!

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:52.980
I'll crush their quick attack power deck!

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.880
Yeah, we can't lose!

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:57.580
We'll show them our strength!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.640
Team Unicorn is a fearsome opponent?

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:06.880
I envy them because it seems they've 
never been in real trouble.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:10.470
They don't know that they're 
going to taste true fear.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.030
That was your fastest time!

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.360
Looks like you're doing well.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:37.590
Sherry!

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.570
Since we're in different blocks, we won't 
meet in the preliminaries.  I came to say hello.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:46.330
So you're also entering?

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:50.230
There are suspicious people 
among the participating teams.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:54.040
They could be Iliaster's assassins.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.040
Be careful.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.010
Sherry.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.930
Stop putting yourself in danger.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:05.250
I told you that there are things I must 
do, even if it means facing danger.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:11.630
Someday, I want to talk to you 
in detail about what we saw.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:20.130
Stay safe throughout the 
preliminaries, Yusei!

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.880
Martha, we came to visit.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:34.610
Oh my!  It's nice for you 
to come, Crow and Jack!

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:36.080
I see.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.950
Yusei couldn't come.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.360
Yeah.  He's busy with repair work.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.060
He wants to finish testing 
the new engine by today.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:50.800
How dare he keep working and not visit 
Martha before the preliminaries!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.280
You should learn from him!

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.170
I heard from Zora that you can't keep a job!

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:00.910
I have no comment regarding that issue.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.880
How are the kids?  They're not here?

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.110
C'mon, you guys!

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.550
Did you forget to say hi to me?

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:21.490
{missing TS}

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:21.490
Did you make this?

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:23.850
They're so much trouble.

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.460
They stayed up late to make it.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:32.220
We're going to bring this 
and cheer for you, Crow!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.950
Crow, do your best!

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.440
You better win!

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.760
He doesn't look like me at all.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.380
I look more like...

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:50.320
Thank you!

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:57.730
Jack, when you start acting like 
an adult, I'll make one for you.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.770
I don't want one!

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.800
Are you jealous?

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:12.880
Bruno, do you know where Crow is?

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:16.350
Crow left for early morning practice.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.580
The highways are empty at this time.

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:24.180
He was full of vigor.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.090
I can still keep going!

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.230
Watch out!

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:49.190
Ouch...

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:50.550
What happened?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.810
You must be kidding!

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.990
There's a crack in my shoulder bone?

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:03.560
Yes.  It will take a month to heal.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:04.730
A month?

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.750
The preliminaries are in three days.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:07.700
You won't heal in time.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.360
Do something!

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.870
I need to enter the tournament!

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.070
But...

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.860
Please!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.880
I don't care if I can never duel again!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.740
I don't care if I lose 
for the rest of my life!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.560
I just want to win this tournament!

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.040
Please do something!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.030
Enough with that nonsense!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:28.520
It's impossible for you 
to enter the tournament!

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:32.120
You quack!  I won't ask 
for your help anymore!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.050
I don't need this cast!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.260
Crow!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:40.230
Damn!  Why now?

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.240
What am I going to tell them?

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:53.610
What should we do?

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.080
Should just the two of us enter?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:19:02.640
According to the tournament rules, if three 
people enter, you duel with 12000 life points.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.820
But if it's two people, its 8000 life points.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.290
That's too big of a handicap.

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:10.260
Are you saying we should give up?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:13.240
No.  We've come too far.

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:14.860
I want to enter.

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:18.810
My philosophy is that if 
I'm entering, I must win!

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.330
I won't duel to lose!

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:25.770
Yusei, Jack.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.520
I'm also a member of Team 5D's.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.240
Let me enter.

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:31.310
Aki?

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.980
Are you serious?

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.080
That's a good idea!

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.720
Having three people is 
definitely more advantageous!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:44.090
I know that I'm an inexperienced D-Wheeler.

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:47.460
But since you're my teammates, 
I want you to accept me.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.160
Please!

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.000
Wait, Crow!

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:57.130
Be quiet!  You can't understand how I feel!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:25.760
I have to toughen up for Yusei, 
Jack and especially Crow.

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:29.020
I have to give it my all!

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:39.180
Crow didn't come home last night.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:42.300
I'm worried.  He was very depressed.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.500
So he just runs off?

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.150
He's like a child!

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:53.090
Izayoi was also just talk!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.820
Aki...

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:03.000
Don't be scared!  Or else, you 
won't be good enough to replace me!

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.810
They made us worry over nothing!

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:11.570
We were overly anxious.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:17.280
Aki, I entrust you with the 
kids' hopes, as well as mine!

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:22.970
The third member of Team 
5D's has been decided.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.780
For the first time since the Fortune Cup,

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:38.570
a huge and exciting Riding Duel event 
has returned to Neo Domino City!

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:13.250
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:18.130
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:23.070
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:28.080
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:33.130
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:39.690
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:43.760
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:49.600
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:53.690
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:59.310
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:02.490
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:04.750
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:09.280
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.250
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:15.690
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:19.070
At our special place
